Dear Regulatory Affairs, Quality Director, Suzhou Site Team,

PRE-APPROVAL INSPECTION (PAI) READINESS.
ANDA 212845 has reached the inspection-decision stage.
An inspection team from CDER's Office of Manufacturing
Quality (OMQ) has been assigned to your Suzhou
facility. This notice summarizes the records that
should be retrievable on-site when investigators
arrive.

1. APPLICATION & FACILITY DETAILS

  Application:       ANDA 212845
  Product:           Metformin HCl Extended-Release
                     Tablets, 500 mg
  Reference Listed
    Drug:            Glucophage XR (NDA 021202)
  Applicant:         Your company, acting through
                     US agent
  Facility:          Suzhou Site (FEI 3011794402)
                     drug product manufacturing
                     & packaging
  Inspection type:   PAI, 4 investigator-days
                     anticipated, OMQ Team 32
  GxP systems in
    scope:           LIMS (Empower 3), MES, batch
                     records (EBR), audit trail
                     review program
  Prior
    correspondence:  IR letter dated 3 Aug 2026;
                     deficiency response submitted
                     29 Sep 2026

2. RECORDS THAT SHOULD BE RETRIEVABLE ON-SITE

  - Batch production & control records,
    exhibit batches 26S-081, 26S-082, 26S-083
  - Audit trail exports (LIMS & EBR,
    1 Jan 2026 - present, unfiltered)
  - Method validation package (assay &
    dissolution, including failed runs)
  - CAPA log (open + closed in last 12 months)
  - Stability data summary (40C/75% RH
    through month 9)

3. HOW THE INSPECTION IS ACTUALLY SCHEDULED

  FDA communicates inspection assignments
  through official written correspondence
  delivered to the applicant's US agent
  (Form FDA 2110 inspection notice and, at
  opening, Form FDA 482 Notice of Inspection).
  Investigators review records ON-SITE in your
  document room with your site personnel.

4. IMPORTANT SECURITY NOTES

  The FDA will NEVER:
  - Ask you to upload batch records, audit
    trails, or any GxP records to a link
    provided in an email
  - Operate a "pre-upload queue", "evidence
    portal", or "PAI pre-review channel"
    outside the Electronic Submissions Gateway
  - Send submission instructions that bypass
    your US agent
  - Cite a "Data Integrity Remediation
    Framework" requiring pre-arrival uploads
  - Threaten refuse-to-receive action based
    on failure to click an email link

  The Electronic Submissions Gateway is
  accessed ONLY by typing the address
  yourself:  accessdata.fda.gov
  (Do not use links from emails. Do not rely
  on the URL shown in a message body.)

  Any message claiming investigators arrive
  "the day after tomorrow" and demanding
  records be uploaded through a portal link
  is a phishing attempt targeting pharma
  regulatory teams before announced
  inspections.

5. IF YOU RECEIVED SUCH A MESSAGE

  - Do not click any link or open any
    attachment
  - Verify inspection scheduling with your
    US agent and your corporate quality office
  - Report suspicious messages to your
    security team and to FDA at
    FDA-OCI@fda.hhs.example

U.S. Food and Drug Administration
Center for Drug Evaluation and Research
Office of Manufacturing Quality
This notice concerns ANDA 212845 only.
